vetica Neue', Arial, Helvetica, 'Nimbus Sans L', sans-serif;color:rgb(119,119,119);font-size:12px;\"><span class=\"meta-prep meta-prep-author\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">Posted on</span> <a href=\"http://www.radia.fm/?p=3555\" title=\"6:00 am\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(119,119,119);\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span class=\"entry-date\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">2015/03/09</span></a> <span class=\"meta-sep\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">by</span> <span class=\"author vcard\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"http://www.radia.fm/?author=35\" title=\"View all posts by CampusParis\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(119,119,119);\" rel=\"nofollow\">CampusParis</a></span></div><div class=\"entry-content\" style=\"background:rgb(255,255,255);border:0px;margin:0px;padding:12px 0px 0px;vertical-align:baseline;clear:both;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Georgia, 'Bitstream Charter', serif;font-size:13.8px;\"><p style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\"><em style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">First 100 days </em>in the sound environment of a new born. With a parliament of crows, bats and birds, family and friends.</p><p style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\"><a href=\"http://www.radia.fm/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/Julia-et-leandre.jpg\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(116,51,153);\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-3556\" title=\"Julia-et-leandre\" src=\"//web.archive.org/web/2im_/http://www.radia.fm/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/Julia-et-leandre.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"background:transparent;border:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;height:auto;\" height=\"388\" width=\"388\" /></a></p><p style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">Julia Drouhin has been working with sound since 2003. She has investigated the haunted air of ghost towns through phono-memory, conducts voodoo sessions with records made of chocolate or ice, has glittered the catacombs of Paris, curated mini-FM events in both France and Spain, and performed with candyfloss clouds. She completed her PhD on the art of walking and radio art at the University of Paris 8 in 2011. In 2014 she won the Giuseppe Englert Prize for which she produced a musical and environmental “Listening Passage” in the mall of Launceston, Tasmania.</p><p style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\"><a href=\"http://www.tacticalmagick.net/juliadrouhin\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(116,51,153);\" rel=\"nofollow\">www.tacticalmagick.net/juliadrouhin</a><br /><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GKY1N0YL4Uw\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(116,51,153);\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GKY1N0YL4Uw</a></p><div><br /></div></div>","licenseurl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/","radiaseason":"34","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.6.3","subject":"radio art;Radia;Campus Paris","title":"Show 0519: First 100 Days by Julia Drouhin (Campus Paris)","publicdate":"2016-11-06 07:48:44","uploader":"radia.fm@gmail.com","addeddate":"2016-11-06 07:48:44","date":"2015-03-09","year":"2015","backup_location":"ia906300_13","external_metadata_update":"2019-04-13T13:04:56Z"},"server":"ia800506.us.archive.org","uniq":89995865,"workable_servers":["ia800506.us.archive.org","ia600506.us.archive.org"]}